From 6f3a8650f8fa2a167bfc28bc28831644947b8216 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Creitin Gameplays <clton999@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 16:07:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/17] diag: one shared console instance, permanent EL2
 header, one-time notifier report

Three fixes to the boot instrumentation, all found from the 2026-11-01 panel photo:

1. The console state was file-scope static, so every translation unit that
   includes diag_stage.h had its own copy.  init/main.c s stage tags and
   printk.c s mirror both looked at a diag_scr_ready that nothing ever set
   and drew nothing, which is why the milestone line stopped at 19 and why
   no printk was mirrored.  There is now one struct diag_console diag_state,
   defined in arch/arm64/kernel/setup.c.

2. Rows 1..3 are permanent and carry the EL2 report (__boot_cpu_mode,
   is_hyp_mode_available(), ID_AA64PFR0_EL1, MIDR): the fact arm64 KVM
   depends on, which otherwise scrolls away with the log.

3. CONFIG_DEBUG_NOTIFIERS (set in the shipping config too) rejects a
   notifier callback that is not in core kernel text, and the stock
   WARN(1, "Invalid notifier called!") then fires at every cpuidle exit -
   burying the log tail under an identical backtrace.  It is replaced by a
   one-time report naming the block and the callback.

Also: the paint bands no longer overwrite the text console once it is up,
and diag/ now carries the generator and the build script, so this
repository can reproduce the instrumentation on its own.
